;
; OVERVIEW
; Bank 3, the normal image of the CS24 chip's second half (port 3DH b2 = 1), visible at
; 4000H-7FFFH when port 31H selects bank 3 for page 1. It is called like a ROM module
; (header at 4000H: reset functions, RAM-disk IOCS, AUTORUN search, device table, file
; handler) and hosts the IM2 interrupt dispatcher (4021H). Code in other banks reaches it
; through RST 18H to 4000H-7FFFH (BANKJP sets port 3DH := 04H); most P0-B0 jump-table
; entries for display, sound, 1500 mode, slots and power go to the jump table at
; 4024H-40EAH. Contents: interrupt dispatcher, LCD character output, keyboard matrix scan
; and key translation, RAM-disk driver and file system (S1:/S2:), COM: file driver and
; serial receive interrupt, PC-1500 (LH5803) CPU switch and 1500 display / math / token
; calls, sound, CALL/OUT/POKE/HEXNUM, work-area allocation, memory map (SSLOTMP, SLOTST,
; APOTST), reset extensions, POWER, WAKE$, EOF/LOF/LOC/DSKF, and the kanji input and font
; code for the JAPAN ROM.
; ============================================================================

