;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 40FCH - IM2 interrupt dispatcher
; P0-B0 INTHND maps bank 3 into page 1 and bank 6 into page 2 and calls 4021H.
; Cause = port 32H AND mask 35H, bits handled in order:
;   b0 serial receive   -> 6488H (COM receive, returns without re-enabling)
;   (others run with only b0 left enabled in 35H, EI, alternate registers)
;   b1 PC-1600 peripheral -> module entry +05H (EXROMCAL L = 05H) of the modules with
;                          F0B2H/F0B3H bits, A = 0
;   b2 PC-1500 peripheral -> INT150 (5CE7H), then clear port 1BH b0
;   b3 LH5803 side      -> acknowledge (port 36H := FBH)
;   b4 1/64 s timer     -> key scan / cursor blink in bank 6 (80ABH/80B7H when F0B6H b7),
;                          modules (F0B6H/F0B7H, A = 2), user hook UH64 (F0BCH)
;                          then port 36H := EFH
;   b6 sub-CPU          -> read SRIRQ (timer IOCS 12H via 8084H), keep masked bits in
;                          TMRMSK, then per event bit (SRIRQ, see IO-Ports §7.1):
;        b1 0.5 s: battery check (IOCS 18H: F0B9H b7 low battery), status symbols
;           (80B1H/80B4H), modules (F0B4H/F0B5H, A = 1), user hook UH05, input
;           status (IOCS 13H -> BINTP1 b7 CI, b0), auto power-off count (APOCNT,
;           reload 1200 = 10 min), F156H counter
;        b0 -> 8075H (analog input / external keyboard)
;        b7 wakeup  -> BINTP1 b6, user hook UHWAKE
;        b6 alarm 1 -> BINTP2 b6, user hook UHALM1
;        b5 alarm 2 -> BINTP2 b7, user hook UHALM2
; Finally the original mask is restored (DI, port 35H).
